            <div xml:id="d297">

                <pb facs="0381" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-18T17:00:00-05:00">April 18, 1933—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. Your 336, April 18, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>First paragraph. This method of approach is apparently much employed and must be
                    guarded against. It affords, however, useful information.</p>
                <p>Second paragraph. Department concurs and approves.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
